  "description": "Was the way I felt about you back then love? Friendship? Or perhaps it was jealousy all along.\n\nBaek Ho-Jin, a former national judo champion, has never experienced the feeling of falling in endlessly—until now. Choi Jeong-Won, a brash magazine editor on the verge of losing his job, stumbles across a fragment of his past: a memory of Baek Ho-Jin, his high school classmate and now one of the nation’s most celebrated heroes.\n\nTasked with securing an exclusive interview with Hojin to save his career, Jeong-Won must navigate old emotions and new challenges. But will he succeed before it’s too late?\"\n\n(Source: Lezhin US)",
